-- title:
--   Eventual reduced-residue hypotheses give cofinal prime AP-count bounds
-- statement:
--   Fix $r,W\in\mathbb N$, $\alpha\ge0$, and nonnegative cut and approximation errors. Let a real polynomial $p$ approximate the positive part on $[-1,1]$ within the approximation error, and assume $2^{2^{r+1}}e_{\rm LF}\le e_{\rm cut}^{\,2^{r+1}}$. Put
--
--   $$
--   e_{\rm dm}=\|p\|_{\rm coeff,1}e_{\rm cut}+e_{\rm app}(2+e_{\rm cut}).
--   $$
--
--   Suppose bounded dense weights have a uniform $(r+2)$-term count lower bound $c_{\rm dense}$ at density $\delta$. Assume nonnegative majorants $\nu_{M,b}$ eventually dominate the prime weights and satisfy the required linear-forms condition uniformly for reduced residues $b$ modulo $W$. Assume also the relative AP-comparison bound with cut error $e_{\rm dm}$ and count error $e_{\rm count}$ whenever $M+1$ is coprime to $(r+1)!$ and the linear-forms condition holds.
--
--   Then beyond every threshold there is a prime modulus $M+1$ such that, for every reduced residue $b$, mean prime weight at least $\delta+e_{\rm dm}$ implies $(r+2)$-term cyclic count at least $c_{\rm dense}-e_{\rm count}$. The same chosen modulus works for all those residues.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs/blob/8822f7ddef30fadbd92e1c6ab4ed897af356af5e/src/latest/Wikipedia/GreenTao/ReducedResidueCofinalTransference.lean#L48-L157

